# Commentor comments for hello.rs
# This file pairs with the source file under .comments.d/<source>.cmt.
# Marker: @N or @N-M, optionally followed by [a=start anchor,b=end anchor].
# Get Commentor: https://commentor.myridia.com/

@1-4 [a=fn step_one(value: i32) -> i32 {,b=doubled_one + 1]
The first function is anchored by its signature and its final expression.
If lines are inserted above it, Commentor finds these same two source lines again.
The marker number is only the readable address; the anchor is the durable link.
This block is deliberately long so the right pane has text to scroll through.
The marker line itself is hidden, while its line position is preserved.
Colour shows which source lines this text belongs to without showing the marker.


@6-9 [a=fn step_two(value: i32) -> i32 {,b=doubled_two + 2]
A short note for the second helper.
Its anchor names two unique lines, so the link stays precise after edits.


@21-24 [a=fn step_three(value: i32) -> i32 {,b=doubled_three + 3]
This marker is intentionally stale for the demo.
The anchor points at step_three near line 11, but the number says line 21.
On open, Commentor should find the irregularity and ask you to review it.
Choose the suggested lines, tick the block, then Apply selected to fix it.
Saving is blocked until the review is applied or skipped.


@16-19 [a=fn step_four(value: i32) -> i32 {,b=doubled_four + 4]


@21-24 [a=fn step_five(value: i32) -> i32 {,b=doubled_five + 5]
Two lines are enough here.
The colour still identifies the binding.


@26-29 [a=fn step_six(value: i32) -> i32 {,b=doubled_six + 6]
This block covers the sixth helper.
It shows that a normal block opens without any review dialog.
The anchor text is stored on the hidden marker line.


@31-34 [a=fn step_seven(value: i32) -> i32 {,b=doubled_seven + 7]
A narrow range with a unique start and end anchor.


@36-39 [a=fn step_eight(value: i32) -> i32 {,b=doubled_eight + 8]
The last helper.
The anchor survives renumbering elsewhere in the file.


@41-50 [a=fn main() {,b=println!("{total}");]
The entry point is anchored by the function signature and the print statement.
The closing brace is deliberately outside the range because it repeats in the file.
If the helpers are edited, this binding should still find main.
